         text="Hypatia, mathematician and the city's most famous philosopher, was seen as the adviser of the prefect Orestes in his feud with the patriarch Cyril. A mob led by a reader named Peter pulled her from her carriage, dragged her into the Caesareum church and killed her with potsherds.",
