         text="By the treaty of November 641 the Byzantine garrison left by sea, and Amr ibn al-As's army marched in eleven months later. Amr is said to have written to the caliph that he had taken a city of 4,000 palaces and 4,000 baths. The capital moved to Fustat on the Nile.",
